<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Monica Daily Growth Brief — 23 July 2026</title></head><body style="margin:0;background:#f3f6f8;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1f2937;line-height:1.45"><div style="max-width:850px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;padding:28px"><div style="border-bottom:5px solid #0f766e;padding-bottom:16px"><div style="font-size:12px;color:#0f766e;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:1px">ALFRED TRAVEL</div><h1 style="margin:5px 0 0;font-size:27px;color:#102a43">Monica Daily Growth Brief</h1><div style="font-size:16px;color:#52606d">User Growth, Activation and Retention</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;color:#52606d">Report date: 23 July 2026 · Prepared at 08:00 AEST</div></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Today’s Growth Decision</h2><div style="background:#fff4e5;border-left:5px solid #d97706;padding:14px 16px"><strong>Do not materially scale acquisition. Maintain controlled acquisition while Engineering repairs the failing itinerary path and Analytics restores event-level measurement and booking attribution.</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">The latest validated complete Metabase window, 13–19 July 2026 UTC, shows 346 real itineraries, 306 ACTIVE outputs and 54 hard failures: 88.4% ACTIVE but 15.6% hard-failure, above the &lt;5% scaling gate. A live Metabase dashboard refresh was available through 22 July for activity presence, but it did not expose a reconciled current reliability funnel. Firebase could not be refreshed because the project/app returned a permission or non-existent-project view; GA4 refreshed successfully for 16–22 July.</p></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Evidence Freshness</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Source</th><th>Evidence window / data through</th><th>Freshness</th><th>What it can support</th></tr><tr><td>Metabase live snapshot</td><td>Runtime dashboard refresh on 23 Jul; activity rows through 22 Jul 2026 UTC</td><td style="color:#166534"><strong>Current snapshot</strong></td><td>Current demand/activity presence and cumulative context; not a complete reliability funnel.</td></tr><tr><td>Metabase latest complete window</td><td>13–19 Jul 2026 UTC; data through 19 Jul</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Recent validated window, 4 days old</strong></td><td>Real itineraries, ACTIVE output and hard-failure calculations.</td></tr><tr><td>Firebase / Jessica event analysis</td><td>Runtime refresh attempted 23 Jul; no readable event window; console returned “project/app does not exist or you do not have permission”</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Current refresh unavailable</strong></td><td>No current activation, D1 retention, Android/iOS retention or push claims. Jessica’s event analysis was unavailable because the Events source was not hydrated/readable.</td></tr><tr><td>GA4</td><td>Last 7 days selected at runtime: 16–22 Jul 2026; data through 22 Jul</td><td style="color:#166534"><strong>Current, mostly complete</strong></td><td>Web users, sessions, page views and source mix; not app retention or downstream booking proof.</td></tr><tr><td>Website and SEO</td><td>Website V2 launched 20 Jul; local assets mtime 20 Jul; observation through 23 Jul</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Early post-launch, 72-hour observation</strong></td><td>Publish state, CTA/indexation surfaces and instrumentation presence; not V2 lift.</td></tr><tr><td>Social / creative intelligence</td><td>Helen’s latest report: 22 Jul; no fresh live social/paid signal verified; data through 22 Jul report boundary</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Access degraded / carry-forward only</strong></td><td>Prior creative direction only; no current performance conclusion.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Growth Scorecard</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Area</th><th>Latest validated result</th><th>Assessment</th><th>Next gate</th></tr><tr><td>Real itinerary demand</td><td>346 real itineraries, 13–19 Jul UTC; [SAMPLE]/internal-test rows excluded</td><td>Demand exists; live snapshot shows continued activity through 22 Jul.</td><td>Fresh 7-day status extract.</td></tr><tr><td>ACTIVE output</td><td>306/346 = <strong>88.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Above 85% broad gate.</td><td>Hold until mode-level failures are repaired.</td></tr><tr><td>Overall hard-failure rate</td><td>54/346 = <strong>15.6%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Reliability blocked.</strong></td><td>&lt;5% on a fresh complete window.</td></tr><tr><td>Primary-mode hard-failure rate</td><td>alfred_plus: 54/94 = <strong>57.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c">Critical path failing.</td><td>&lt;5% with route/provider/reason reconciliation.</td></tr><tr><td>Cleanest-performing mode</td><td>Mode taxonomy incomplete in latest extract; broad non-alfred_plus comparison not causal</td><td>Do not over-credit the apparent clean path.</td><td>Normalize mode coverage.</td></tr><tr><td>Day-1 retention</td><td>Current Firebase event-level result unavailable; no valid overall value</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Hydrated cohort result.</td></tr><tr><td>Android retention</td><td>Current Firebase result unavailable</td><td>Measurement blocked; do not infer from DAU.</td><td>Android D1 and return-session cohort.</td></tr><tr><td>iOS retention</td><td>Current Firebase result unavailable</td><td>Measurement blocked; do not infer from DAU.</td><td>iOS D1 and return-session cohort.</td></tr><tr><td>Push-notification performance</td><td>Current Firebase event/campaign result unavailable</td><td>No performance conclusion.</td><td>FCM delivered/opened → return session.</td></tr><tr><td>Trustworthy bookings</td><td>No current unique-confirmation reconciliation available</td><td>Do not count duplicate or unreconciled confirmations.</td><td>100% journey-linked unique IDs.</td></tr><tr><td>Sample-data pollution</td><td>Excluded from 346 production itineraries; live dashboard shows 1,849 sample itineraries cumulative</td><td>Sample population is material and must remain segregated.</td><td>Daily sample share in every KPI extract.</td></tr><tr><td>Organic acquisition</td><td>GA4 16–22 Jul: 27 active users from google/organic; 34 Organic Search sessions</td><td>Meaningful web signal, but Website V2 cutover began 20 Jul.</td><td>Join organic source to qualified generation and ACTIVE.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">What is Working</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Signal</th><th>Evidence</th><th>How Monica should use it</th></tr><tr><td>Current activity remains present</td><td>Metabase live snapshot refreshed at runtime; cumulative dashboard showed 3,298 new users and 3,517 itineraries in the trailing 365-day cards, with rows through 22 Jul.</td><td>Protect the existing demand base; do not buy more volume until quality is proven.</td></tr><tr><td>Broad output is near the operational gate</td><td>306 ACTIVE / 346 real = 88.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Use as a recovery benchmark, not scale permission.</td></tr><tr><td>Web acquisition has an organic base</td><td>GA4 16–22 Jul: 27 google/organic active users and 34 Organic Search sessions.</td><td>Prioritise qualified organic landing paths and downstream measurement.</td></tr><tr><td>Website V2 has usable conversion surfaces</td><td>Website V2 launched 20 Jul; local index and analytics assets were present through 23 Jul.</td><td>Observe CTA and indexation behaviour for 7 days before claiming lift.</td><tr><td>Creative direction is actionable</td><td>Helen’s 22 Jul report carried forward family-constraint → personalised itinerary and Japan-with-kids utility angles; no fresh live validation.</td><td>Use only as capped hypotheses, not as performance proof.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Largest Growth Leaks</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Leak</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Business impact</th></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>alfred_plus generation reliability</td><td>54/94 hard failures = 57.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Users fail before activation; acquisition spend is wasted.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Overall reliability above gate</td><td>54/346 = 15.6%, 13–19 Jul UTC vs &lt;5% required.</td><td>Planner trust and repeat use are at risk.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Activation and retention observability</td><td>Firebase refresh unavailable on 23 Jul; Events explorer was not hydrated/readable.</td><td>Cannot identify platform-specific leaks or prove retention.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Booking attribution</td><td>No current unique confirmation-to-itinerary/user reconciliation.</td><td>Monetization and payback cannot guide channel scaling.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Web-to-product reconciliation</td><td>GA4 16–22 Jul is session/user based; Metabase 13–19 Jul is itinerary grain; no current user-level join.</td><td>Cannot rank channels by qualified downstream value.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Fresh creative intelligence</td><td>Helen reported no new live social/paid signal verified on 22 Jul.</td><td>Creative decisions remain hypothesis-led.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Seven-Day Action Plan</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Action</th><th>Owner</th><th>Success measure</th><th>Scaling gate</th></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Triage alfred_plus by route, provider, timeout and response reason; add safe fallback.</td><td>Engineering</td><td>alfred_plus hard-failure &lt;5% in a fresh complete 7-day window.</td><td>Keep acquisition controlled until met.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Restore Firebase access and hydrate the canonical event table: signup → first_open → generate → ACTIVE → view/save/share → return.</td><td>Jessica / Analytics</td><td>Row-level validation overall, Android and iOS; current data-through date recorded.</td><td>Measurement unblocked only after event reconciliation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Reconcile booking confirmation IDs to itinerary and user journey; deduplicate writes.</td><td>Data Engineering</td><td>100% counted bookings have one unique confirmation ID and journey mapping.</td><td>No monetization scaling claim before pass.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Join GA4 source/session to signup, qualified generation and ACTIVE at user/cohort grain.</td><td>Growth Analytics</td><td>One source-by-platform table with qualified generation and ACTIVE rate.</td><td>Scale only channels with validated downstream activation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Improve first-week return after successful itinerary and validate notifications.</td><td>Product / CRM</td><td>Fresh D1 and 7-day return by platform; FCM delivered/opened measured.</td><td>Controlled messaging until retention is stable.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P2</strong></td><td>Run a capped Website V2 family-constraint CTA test after instrumentation check.</td><td>Jessica / Growth</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation per organic session, with ACTIVE and failure guardrails.</td><td>Expand only after 7-day post-launch baseline.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Recommended Growth Experiments</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Experiment</th><th>Proposition</th><th>Primary success metric</th><th>Secondary metrics</th></tr><tr><td>Reliable-path CTA test</td><td>Route qualified web visitors to the validated itinerary path, not the failing alfred_plus path.</td><td>Qualified generation → successful ACTIVE itinerary rate.</td><td>CTA click, webapp arrival, hard failures, time to ACTIVE.</td></tr><tr><td>First-plan return prompt</td><td>After ACTIVE, prompt one practical next action: view, save or share.</td><td>Return session within 7 days.</td><td>Itinerary view, save/share, D1 by platform.</td></tr><tr><td>Intent-led Website V2 test</td><td>Compare family/multi-city logistics copy with generic AI-planning copy after wiring is validated.</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation per organic session.</td><td>CTA click, ACTIVE output, booking intent, hard-failure guardrail.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Billy’s Decisions Today</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Decision required</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr><tr><td>Acquisition budget</td><td>Approve controlled acquisition only; no material paid scaling until hard-failure is &lt;5% on a fresh complete window and activation, retention and attribution are validated.</td></tr><tr><td>P0 ownership</td><td>Assign Engineering, Jessica/Analytics and Data Engineering owners with this week’s dates for alfred_plus, Firebase access and booking reconciliation.</td></tr><tr><td>Website V2 readout</td><td>Approve a 7-day post-launch baseline; treat 20–23 Jul as observation, not proof of conversion lift.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Overall Status</h2><p style="font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#b91c1c;border-top:3px solid #b91c1c;padding-top:12px">Growth status: Reliability blocked</p><p>Demand and web acquisition are visible, but the latest validated reliability window fails the scaling gate and Firebase event-level evidence is unavailable. The correct next move is reliability, measurement and booking attribution recovery before material acquisition expansion.</p><p style="font-size:11px;color:#667085;border-top:1px solid #d0d5dd;padding-top:10px">Evidence note: rates independently recalculated from the 13–19 Jul Metabase extract; [SAMPLE] and internal/test rows excluded. GA4 is current for 16–22 Jul. Firebase is explicitly unavailable for refreshed decisioning. Current snapshots are not treated as complete funnels.</p></div></body></html>
